# Mobile update workflow (required after mobile changes)

When finishing work that touches `mobile/` (apps, packages, Android, or shared API client), do **all** of the following before stopping. Do not skip APKs unless the user explicitly says so.

## 1. Localhost preview (web)

Follow [localhost-refresh](localhost-refresh.mdc):

- Run the app under edit with `flutter run -d web-server --web-port=5050 --web-hostname=127.0.0.1` (fallback port OK).
- Never open Chrome/Edge. Refresh Cursor IDE browser at `http://127.0.0.1:5050`.
- Prefer hot restart / same process if already running.

## 2. WiFi debugging → update phone

ADB: `D:\Android\Sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe` (or `$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Android\Sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe` if present).

1. Run `adb devices -l`.
2. If a device is listed (USB or WiFi `IP:port`), **install** the apps you changed:
   - Passenger: `adb -s <serial> install -r mobile/apks/can-go-passenger-local.apk` (local testing) **or** `…-release.apk` when verifying live.
   - Driver: same with `can-go-driver-local.apk` / `can-go-driver-release.apk`.
3. Default when WiFi debug is up and local backend is the target: install the **local** APKs.
4. If no device: note that and still produce the 4 APKs.

## 3. Always build 4 release APKs

Build **one APK at a time** (never parallel passenger+driver or local+live). Do not run `gradlew --stop` or kill Java/Dart while a build is running.

Copy into `mobile/apks/`:

| File | App | `CANGO_API_BASE` |
|------|-----|------------------|
| `can-go-passenger-local.apk` | passenger | `http://<LAN_IP>:4000/api` |
| `can-go-passenger-release.apk` | passenger | `https://www.can-rides.ca/api` |
| `can-go-driver-local.apk` | driver | `http://<LAN_IP>:4000/api` |
| `can-go-driver-release.apk` | driver | `https://www.can-rides.ca/api` |

**LAN IP for local APKs:** prefer the host IPv4 on the same subnet as the phone (often `192.168.100.x`). Never bake `127.0.0.1` into phone APKs — the device cannot reach the PC that way.

```powershell
$adb = "D:\Android\Sdk\platform-tools\adb.exe"
$lan = (Get-NetIPAddress -AddressFamily IPv4 |
  Where-Object { $_.IPAddress -like '192.168.*' -and $_.IPAddress -notlike '*.1' } |
  Select-Object -First 1 -ExpandProperty IPAddress)
if (-not $lan) { $lan = "192.168.100.5" }
$localApi = "http://${lan}:4000/api"
$liveApi = "https://www.can-rides.ca/api"
$apks = "d:\xampp\htdocs\get-transfer\mobile\apks"
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $apks | Out-Null

# Passenger local + live
cd "d:\xampp\htdocs\get-transfer\mobile\apps\passenger"
flutter build apk --release --dart-define=CANGO_API_BASE=$localApi
Copy-Item "build\app\outputs\flutter-apk\app-release.apk" "$apks\can-go-passenger-local.apk" -Force
flutter build apk --release --dart-define=CANGO_API_BASE=$liveApi
Copy-Item "build\app\outputs\flutter-apk\app-release.apk" "$apks\can-go-passenger-release.apk" -Force

# Driver local + live
cd "d:\xampp\htdocs\get-transfer\mobile\apps\driver"
flutter build apk --release --dart-define=CANGO_API_BASE=$localApi
Copy-Item "build\app\outputs\flutter-apk\app-release.apk" "$apks\can-go-driver-local.apk" -Force
flutter build apk --release --dart-define=CANGO_API_BASE=$liveApi
Copy-Item "build\app\outputs\flutter-apk\app-release.apk" "$apks\can-go-driver-release.apk" -Force
```

Tell the user the four APK paths and which one was installed on the device (if any).

## When this does NOT apply

- Pure backend/admin/web-only changes with **no** `mobile/` edits — skip APKs unless the user asks.
- User explicitly says skip builds / skip device install.
